computePolicyChange: for each descendant entity (isWithin(e.groupId,gid)): from=effective(e).value; to=effective(e,{groupId:gid,value}).value; changed if differ. Note: for entities that have own status → unaffected. For entities under nearer policy (between entity and gid there's another group with policy) → override at gid doesn't affect. effective(e, override) checks override only when walking chain at matching group — nearer policies earlier in chain (self→root) return before reaching gid... wait chain is self→root order: nearer groups come FIRST. So if a nearer group has policy, we return it before reaching the override group. ✓ Correct semantics.

But subtle: override.value='none' (clearing policy) → override means "policy is null at that group". Handle: in effective(), at matching group use override.value which may be null → skip (continue). ✓ Implementation: `const pol = (ov && ov.groupId===g.id) ? ov.value : g.policy; if(pol) return ...` ✓.

